# Create a directory for your OE-Core setup to live in and clone the meta-information:
```sh
https://github.com/silmates/linux-silmates.git -b <branch_name>
```
# here we take reference from TI for sm-ti-6.1.y branch:- 
https://git.ti.com/git/ti-linux-kernel/ti-linux-kernel.git -b ti-linux-6.1.y

## Without interrupting URL by giving ID and password Configure below steps :-

# Generate SSH-keys:
```sh
ssh-keygen -t rsa -b 4096 -C "<your gitlab mail id>" -f ~/.ssh/<mycustom_rsa>
```

# Enter the key installation path (/home/user/.ssh/<key_name>) and add SSH-key to SSH-agent:
```sh
ssh-add ~/.ssh/<key_name>
```

# Copy SSH Key to Clipboard:
```sh
cat ~/.ssh/<key_name.pub>
```

# Add keys to your GIT-LAB:
```sh 
   I)   login to your git-hub
   II)  user setting --> ssh key genration 
   III) add key  
``` 
